From f94b17476e38371fbf6038eaa520bcba11c03601 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@mabn.pl>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 07:54:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] headless demo replay: skip eager piece-transform walk in
 TickAllAnims

The BFS pass at the end of TickAllAnims eagerly recomputes every dirty
piece's piece-space/model-space transforms and sets the wasUpdated and
(via SetFloat3's dirty-transition check) boundaries-recalc flags - all
rendering plumbing. Synced consumers never depend on the eager walk:
weapon aiming, script callouts and Lua GetUnitPiece* read through
GetModelSpaceTransform()/GetModelSpaceMatrix(), whose lazy
UpdateParentMatricesRec computes identical values on demand (the engine
already relies on that equivalence - those readers run between walks all
the time). Under HEADLESS && hostDemo, skip the walk entirely; dirty
pieces get resolved lazily by whoever reads them, or never, if nothing
does.

Flag-level consequences (pieces staying dirty longer, wasUpdated not
set, boundary recalcs firing on a different cadence) all land in
draw-only state: every GetDrawRadius / boundingVolume / wasUpdated
reader lives under Rendering/. Verified byte-identical output via the
snapshot-diff gate.

TickAllAnims was still 9.5% inclusive (main thread) post-H2, with the
walk visiting every piece of every animating model every sim frame.
---
 rts/Sim/Units/Scripts/UnitScript.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rts/Sim/Units/Scripts/UnitScript.cpp b/rts/Sim/Units/Scripts/UnitScript.cpp
index 0af3ef8..3b0099d 100644
--- a/rts/Sim/Units/Scripts/UnitScript.cpp
+++ b/rts/Sim/Units/Scripts/UnitScript.cpp
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #ifndef _CONSOLE
 
 #include "Game/GameHelper.h"
+#include "Game/GameSetup.h"
 #include "Game/GlobalUnsynced.h"
 #include "Map/Ground.h"
 #include "Sim/Misc/GlobalSynced.h"
@@ -235,6 +236,20 @@ void CUnitScript::TickAllAnims(int deltaTime)
 	// [barreplay] order-preserving erase (was swap-erase VectorEraseIfAll), so a
 	// sorted <anims> stays sorted and the per-tick sort above can stay skipped
 	std::erase_if(anims, [](const auto& ai) { return ai.done; });
+
+#ifdef HEADLESS
+	// [barreplay] the walk below eagerly recomputes every dirty piece's
+	// transforms and sets the wasUpdated / boundaries-recalc flags - all of it
+	// for the benefit of rendering. Synced readers (weapon aim, script
+	// callouts, Lua GetUnitPiece*) never rely on it: they go through the lazy
+	// GetModelSpaceTransform()/GetModelSpaceMatrix() path, whose
+	// UpdateParentMatricesRec computes the exact same values on demand - the
+	// engine already depends on that equivalence, since those readers run
+	// between walks. In a headless demo replay nothing draws, so skip the
+	// eager walk; pieces stay dirty until a synced reader actually needs them.
+	if (gameSetup != nullptr && gameSetup->hostDemo)
+		return;
+#endif
 #if 1
 	// BFS pass
 	// [barreplay] reuses a per-thread scratch buffer instead of constructing a
